  "findings": [
    "Anchored command is tried after note and before meta. It mutates existing entity/package/note URL fields and creates no entity/UID. Entity.addUrl replaces the Java URL, so replacement is correct. Recovered named-note controls retain class, note and relationships in the independent YAML captures.",
    "The reused resolver differs from Java: unique lookup must reject the current group itself and fall back to its child; Rust does not. Root entity_by_path early return can also bypass Java context resolution. Supplemental current-group, root/ambiguous and namespace controls probe these exact branches; this is source evidence, not a blanket verdict on every URL control.",
    "F3-note-only-url-dropped: The parser correctly replaces URL and tooltip and retains sole Note UID, but render_notes_only dispatches to render_single_named_note, which never calls note_anchor or emits an anchor. Java EntityImageNote draws the existing note-owned URL inside the entity group even on the degenerated path. Whole input mismatch despite correct YAML.",
    "F4-url-smart-quotes: Pattern2 substitutes %g with ASCII plus curly/invisible double quotes. CommandUrl and UrlBuilder share this grammar. Rust try_url and BUILDERS accept only ASCII quotes. Java exits0 with valid diagram; Rust exits1 unrecognized command.",
    "F5-current-group-self: CucaDiagram.quarkInContextSafe(true) excludes byName==currentQuark and resolves its child; that child is absent so Java exits200. Rust ReuseUnique returns current group and try_url mutates its URL, exit0. This is invalid-input acceptance, not a valid SVG pass.",
    "F6-invalid-path-filtered: Java badName rejects the repeated separator; Rust split_identity filters empty components and updates Basin.Anchor, exit0 where Java exits200.",
    "F7-root-scope-identity: Java renders distinct Memo and Basin.Memo and attaches URL to the local class/note. Rust early root entity_by_path reuse merges class declarations or rejects the local named note as already created. Existing shared resolver/creation mismatch predates the new command; valid-input process error persists, and new URL consumption depends on that incorrect model.",
    "F8-rooted-command-residue: Java retains extra entity Basin.url (ent0005) alongside Basin.Other and root Memo, while Rust retains only two entities. Both attach URL to root Memo. CommandLinkClass precedes CommandUrl in Java factory; the precise multi-pass side effect has not been instrumented. Retain full failure as unresolved command/model ownership, not geometry/environment.",
    "F9-group-geometry-and-inline-ownership: Single-line Java CommandFactoryNoteOnEntity passes null URL; Rust emits extra anchor. Multiline both own one anchor but Java note text x184.46 versus Rust182.46, canvas338 versus336 without external link and246 versus244 with link. Geometry fails independently of anchor ownership. No fresh native solve or global environment claim.",
    "Independent real release CLI replay: preserved1649 990\u21921004 matches; maker26 2\u219220; zero lost passes/new valid process errors. These1675 entries contain1601 unique source hashes; smaller cohorts overlap and are not additive.",
    "Independent fresh86:36 pass,17 mismatch,2 valid-input process errors,31 invalid Java references.55 Java-valid inputs;36/55 match. The29 explicit-class controls are24 pass/5 mismatch. Original no-allowmixing controls remain preserved separately.",
    "Main exact-candidate library tiers:11188/11251 product and10523/11251 assisted, both exit101. Guards4/6, clippy20 diagnostics remain red.1444 unit and34 CLI/doc/error tests plus fmt pass. Neither main tier is a CLI headline.",
    "All prior584 independent evidence files are byte-identical. No historic account/review/pair or production/baseline/comparator/skip/target/policy was edited. Source account commit ancestry is established, but corrective-account descriptions of v1/v3 drafts prevent certifying a literal before-any-code-written chronology.",
